s  um so we can see uh you know here is an  area between curves  query um and this is one of our brand  new step-by-step features that we've  added um  i think just this spring so here we have  our  you know the the hints and the steps  that you would see on the website but  uh here we have them in line in the  notebook  and then you can kind of go through and  see  what the answer ends up being some of  our other steps programs that we have  we have angle between curves and we  added a couple new ones  both this norm vector norm  and some limit definition derivative  steps  um these two are extra exciting because  they were added by interns that we had  over the summer  oh well congratulations to them that's a  pretty cool accomplishment  yeah so you know just a few short months  here they're able to add  a step-by-step program not just for the  wolfram alpha website but it's also  working  in the notebook environment as well  excellent so  so these step-by-steps they look  very nice is is that the main point uh  or are there any  is there anything you can pull from  these that you can compute on further or  are these sort of just  self-contained little uh sort of  tutorials  if that makes sense right yeah the the  step-by-step themselves are  are designed to kind of walk you through  how a human  uh or a student studying that material  um  how they might compute that uh if  they're doing it by hand  so there's not really anything we can do  to kind of chain this in with another  query  um but uh you know  right but in theory you could you could  go through these steps and wolfram alpha  would understand  you know if you're entering it in there  you could get a lot of those same  yeah and if you're in results if you're  not asking first steps you can  you can ask for just the angle between  the vectors and you can get that  end result then and then do subsequent  computations with it  okay makes sense  all right so so what else uh aside from  the step-by-step what 